    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Floodplains are flat, fertile land areas located directly beside river channels.",
        "Natural levees are raised river banks formed naturally during flood events.",
        "Meanders represent winding, looping bends along the course of a river.",
        "Oxbow lakes originate when meander loops are cut off from the main river flow.",
        "Alluvial fans build up as cone-shaped sediment deposits at mountain foothills.",
        "Deltas form triangular depositional features where the river meets its mouth."
      ],
      "id": "tqdo6jp"
